{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtQKEKepV2tS4PHEi16B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane, under `sandbox/agent.sb` with a scratch HOME, as the kimi lane does. I did not run it end to end, because that sends the task to OpenAI. The sandbox pieces and the CLI start-up were checked directly.\n\n**What changed**\n- `run.sh`: new `codex_sandboxed_run`. Codex's config and login live in a scratch `CODEX_HOME`. Its `-o` output goes to `/tmp`, and the lane copies `final.txt` into the run folder afterwards. If that file is missing, it notes this in `agent.err`, because Codex exits 0 either way.\n- `README.md`: lane list updated.\n- `ANSWER.md`: what I did, which parts of the colleague's note applied, verification, and known gaps.\n\n**Verification:** `bash -n` passes. Under the profile, `codex --version` runs, reads of the real `~/.codex/config.toml` are denied, and writes to scratch in `/tmp` succeed.\n\n**Colleague's note:** The `-o` write failure only happens when the run folder is under the real home. Here `runs/` is under `/private/tmp`, so the failure probably wouldn't have occurred. I still used the scratch pattern and the missing-file check, since they cost nothing. The Mistral Vibe parts don't apply because this repo has no such lane.\n\n**Gaps to know about:**\n- **Login token is visible to the agent's shell.** Codex logs in through `~/.codex/auth.json`, not an env key. The lane copies that file into scratch, so the sandboxed shell can read it during the run. The rest of the home stays blocked. Moving to an API-key env var would close this, but the README says Codex uses an env key and `CODEX_API_KEY` isn't set here, so I didn't change the auth setup.\n- **Config isn't copied.** `config.toml` holds MCP server entries, so this lane runs with default Codex config while the `codex` lane uses yours. Results may differ if model or MCP settings matter.\n- **Token refreshes are lost** with the scratch folder.\n\nNext step: `./run.sh <task> codex-sandboxed`, then check that `final.txt` is non-empty and `agent.err` has no \"no last message\" line."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2393,"cache_read_input_tokens":37108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2393},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1001038b-e3cf-421d-9d4e-e2a13d88ae49","uuid":"8e6d41bd-188b-4450-8baa-f740ee5a4e6b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:45:59.519Z","request_id":"req_011CgtQKE7znq1ZKTAQYMea2"}
